{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_bdrk_taj46z6nynrovrim3ab7vjenht23atlnbz53tqg7ih7pi2e6xhka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All phases are complete. Let me provide a final summary of the work.\n\n## Summary\n\nI verified the C-to-Rust translation of **PCRE2 10.48 (8-bit, SUPPORT_UNICODE)** by building both libraries as shared objects and differentially testing them through the FFI boundary via `libloading`.\n\n### Build configuration\n- **Cargo.toml has no `[features]` section** → exactly one valid configuration (default). `cargo check --no-default-features` also passes, so there is a single code path to verify. Added `libloading = \"0.8\"` to `[dev-dependencies]`.\n\n### Bug fixes (Rust changed, C never touched)\n1. **`pcre2_substitute.rs` had a truncated duplicate.** The file contained a complete `pcre2_substitute_8` (lines 734–1979) plus its helpers, then a *second, incomplete* copy that was cut off mid-function, causing an unclosed-delimiter compile error. Removed the duplicate; `cargo check`/`build` now succeed.\n2. **`pcre2_dfa_match.rs` misaligned-pointer UB.** The base recursion workspace was declared `[c_int; N]` (4-byte aligned) and cast to `*mut RWS_anchor` (which holds a pointer, needing 8-byte alignment) — matching the C's `int[]`→`RWS_anchor*` cast, but Rust's debug alignment checks aborted. Wrapped it in a `#[repr(align(8))]` struct so the cast is sound while preserving identical behavior.\n\n### Phase A — surface mapped\n- **SYMBOLS.md**: all 143 `nm -D` symbols; `diff` confirms **identical symbol sets** (0 missing, 0 extra) for both debug and release `.so`.\n- **ERRORS.md**: 46 distinct rejection rows across all public entry points.\n- **CONFIGS.md**: 41 valid-configuration rows spanning compile/match/dfa options, input shapes, UTF/UCP, substring, substitute, serialize, maketables, config.\n\n### Phases B/C — differential tests (24 tests, all passing)\n- **phase_b_valid.rs** (5): compile+match matrix (literals, quantifiers, anchors, alternation, captures, named groups, classes, caseless/multiline/dotall/extended, backrefs, look-arounds), match-option flags, UTF/UCP, empty subjects/ovector sizes, and DFA matching — each with 80–200 seeded-random inputs comparing rc + full ovector + startchar byte-for-byte.\n- **phase_b_valid2.rs** (8): pattern_info selectors, substring copy/get/length by number & name, substitute (plain/global/literal/case-forcing/named/default/overflow/replacement-only), serialize encode→decode→re-match, config selectors, maketables (verified 1088-byte table identity), get_error_message.\n- **phase_c_errors.rs** (11): every ERRORS.md row — bad config/compile options, NULL/BADOFFSET/BADOPTION on match & dfa_match, invalid UTF, unset limits, substring NOSUBSTRING/UNSET/UNAVAILABLE/NOMEMORY, substitute BADOPTION/NOMEMORY/BADREPLACEMENT/REPMISSINGBRACE/NOSUBSTRING, serialize errors, and out-of-range enum/selector values passed across FFI.\n\n### Completion gate\n- ✅ Symbol diff empty (143/143, both profiles)\n- ✅ Every CONFIGS.md row passes across randomized inputs\n- ✅ Every ERRORS.md row has a passing error-path differential test\n- ✅ Only one build configuration exists (no features), and it holds\n\n`run_tests.sh` automates the required rebuild-then-test flow (the standalone cdylib must be rebuilt with `cargo build` before `cargo test`, since the harness loads the `.so` rather than linking the crate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":438,"cache_read_input_tokens":118996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":438,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8126b15b-3371-4d8b-bb4f-93920776cb73","uuid":"d1ff5542-51d8-454a-a9d4-97f4f3375bea","timestamp":"2026-08-05T06:45:29.613Z"}
